Z||000002||88formula||03-26-2001||08:00 PM||||The 88 flywheel is neutrally balanced. I have to get my engine back together to let you know how far the flywheel sticks out of the block. There are a lot of places I can use as a reference for that measurement. Why do you want to know that?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||florid87gt||03-26-2001||08:11 PM||||I need to know because I will need the 88 flywheel to stick the same amount inback of my adaptor plate as is it does on the engine originally. that way I won't have to make any changes for the throw out bearing and linkage. the distance I am looking for is the distance from the mounting surface of the trans to the clutch surface. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||florid87gt||03-27-2001||09:52 PM||||doesn't anyone have a 2.8 out with a flywheel on it? if someone could measure from the clutch surface of the flywheel to the mounting surface of the engine/trans it would be most appreciated Thanks.<p>[This message has been edited by florid87gt (edited 03-27-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000005||rockcrawl||03-27-2001||10:13 PM||||I can get you the measurement tomorow when I have daylight.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rockcrawl||03-28-2001||09:10 PM||||The 2.8 flywheel is .815" thick from mounting surface to clutch contact surface. The 2.5 measures about .805". The crankshaft sticks out past the back of the block very little, maybe .00-.10", and I've seen a lot of variation between different engines. Depends a lot on crank end-play, bearing condition, etc.. I think .05" would be a good # to use.<P>I just read elsewhere that the V6 flywheel is .840" thick. Not sure if this is someones measurement or a factory spec. Still very close to my measurement.<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 03-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||florid87gt||03-28-2001||10:05 PM||||OK just so we are on the same page. If I were to take a straight edge and place across a flywheel that doesn't have a clutch mounted yet and measure back to the engine/trans mounting surface it would be about .820 to .915. Actually I don't need exact precision just +/- .25. Thanks!<P>[This message has been edited by florid87gt (edited 03-28-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by florid87gt (edited 03-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||rockcrawl||03-29-2001||06:09 PM||||Yes, you've got it. But i'd keep it closer to .820 - .860||||reg||1
